    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW26aCS35HEk4KLeWC6uGk8ex)_\n\n## What\n- 41 litnotes stayed in the `sp-litnotes-meta-fill-all` report after `A`.\n\n## Causes and fixes\n- **`update pub-author` (André/Andre, Søren/Soren, Ştefan/Ștefan, DeMarco/Demarco, ...)**\n  - The link text is the person note's title and the write keeps the link, but the diff compared it exactly with the BibTeX spelling.\n  - Fix: person names are compared without accents, case and extra spaces; a really different name is still an update.\n- **`fill bib-parent` + `order the meta lines`**\n  - The plan filled bib-parent whenever the crossref was set, even when it has no note and no BibTeX entry, so nothing was ever written.\n  - The order check assumed that line would be added, so it always said \"unsorted\".\n  - Fix: such a crossref is not planned; it is listed under \"Crossref without a note or a BibTeX entry\".\n  - Keys with a colon (`marx1966cartea-i:-`) were split by the notes index and never found; they are found now.\n- **`arthur-1998-fluid-capit` / `arthur-2022-reprod` (nothing applied at all)**\n  - Likely a whole-note failure (unsaved buffer, or an error while making the parent), which was only counted.\n  - Fix: an error on one line no longer loses the others, and failures are listed under \"Problems in the last convert\".\n\n## Tests\n- `tests/sp-litnotes-meta-test.el`: 5 new tests, 61/61 pass on Emacs 29.3; `sp-author-notes*`, `-refs`, `sp-batch-report` pass.\n- `sp-litnotes-titles-bib-authors-surname` fails on main too, unrelated.\n- Docs: edited `docs/tangles/academic/sp-litnotes-meta.org` and `docs/tangles/funct/sp-org-lint.org` (tangled sources). No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9KR7XnCfG9uwLXz4k)_",
